def:
A DR drill (Disaster Recovery drill) is a planned simulation where we test our disaster recovery strategy by assuming real outage scenarios 
such as region failure, data center outage, or application crash. The objective is to verify that we can restore services within
defined RTO and RPO targets.

During the drill, we validate backups, trigger failover to the DR environment, bring up infrastructure using IaC tools like Terraform, 
restore applications and databases, perform health checks, and monitor alerts. We measure recovery time, document gaps, and 
update runbooks to improve reliability.

Regular DR drills ensure business continuity, reduce downtime, and improve operational readiness during real disasters.
______________________________________________________________________
how we perform this:

Step-by-Step DR Drill Procedure
1️⃣ Define Objectives

Identify critical applications & services

Define RTO (Recovery Time Objective) and RPO (Recovery Point Objective)

Decide drill type:

Partial (single app)

Full DR (entire region)

2️⃣ Plan & Communicate

Schedule drill (monthly/quarterly)

Inform:

Dev teams

Business stakeholders

Support teams

Prepare DR runbook

Take management approval

3️⃣ Validate Backups

Verify:

Database snapshots

EBS volume backups

S3 replication

Perform test restore in DR environment

4️⃣ Simulate Disaster

Intentionally:

Stop primary services

Block network

Scale down cluster

This mimics:

Region outage

Application failure

5️⃣ Trigger Failover

Switch traffic using:

Route53 failover routing

Load balancer DNS change

Activate:

DR region

Standby cluster

6️⃣ Restore Infrastructure

Using Terraform/IaC:

Create:

VPC

EKS / EC2

RDS replicas

Attach:

Storage

Security groups

7️⃣ Restore Applications

Deploy:

Application pods

ConfigMaps

Secrets

Restore:

Database from snapshot

Persistent volumes

8️⃣ Validate Services

Check:

Application URLs

API health

DB connectivity

Perform:

Smoke testing

Sample transactions

9️⃣ Monitor & Alert Validation

Confirm:

Prometheus metrics

Grafana dashboards

Slack/PagerDuty alerts

🔟 Measure RTO & RPO

Track:

Total recovery time

Data loss window

Compare with SLA targets

1️⃣1️⃣ Failback (Optional)

Switch traffic back to primary

Sync data

Restore normal operations

1️⃣2️⃣ Documentation & Improvement

Prepare:

DR drill report

RCA

Identify:

Gaps

Automation improvements

Update runbooks

🔹 Short Interview Version

We define scope and RTO/RPO, validate backups, simulate outage, trigger failover to DR site, restore infra using Terraform, 
deploy applications, validate services, monitor alerts, measure recovery time, perform failback, and document findings.
